# Levels

| Level | Tool | Covers |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Unit | Vitest | Business logic, decision calculations, scoring, Zod validators |
| Integration | Vitest | Adapters against the real thing: `database` against PostgreSQL, `ai` against a provider |
| Workflow | Vitest | A full engine run from submission to `STORED`, `FAILED`, or `REJECTED` |
| End to end | Vitest | Run the built CLI against a test database and a fake provider: `decide`, `approve`, `reject`, `resume`, `show`, `eval` |

Playwright joins for the web app in Phase 2 (ADR-018).

# Rules

- Colocate unit and integration tests as `*.test.ts` next to the code. Put end-to-end tests in `tests/`.
- Unit and workflow tests never call a real model. Pass a fake `AIProvider` that returns fixed, schema-valid output.
- Provider integration tests are opt-in by environment variable, so CI and local runs stay free and deterministic by default.
- Test the database through real PostgreSQL (a local container or a Neon branch), never a mocked client. Run migrations first.
- Always cover the critical paths: decision classification, expert selection, council composition per impact level, consensus calculation, memory retrieval, and run recovery.
- Every failure mode in `docs/10-architecture/system-design.md#failure-modes` has a workflow test: invalid model output, partial expert failure, interrupted run and `resume`, database unavailable, pending and rejected approval.
- Every model-output schema has a test showing it rejects malformed output.
- Assert on behavior and stored results, not on prompt wording or call order.
- When fixing a bug, first add a test that fails without the fix.
- Coverage percentage is not a goal. An untested critical path blocks the pull request.

# Example

❌ A consensus test that calls the real model and asserts `agreement > 0.5`.

✅ A consensus test that feeds 5 fixed votes (4 for, 1 against, known weights) into the scoring function and asserts the exact agreement value.

